    "https://viterbo.applicantpro.com/jobs/4217966": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Business",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Business. Viterbo University. Viterbo University's Dahl School of Business is seeking a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Business. This position begins August 2027. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to student-centered teaching, applied learning, ethical leadership, and the mission of Viterbo University, a Catholic, Franciscan institution. This position is based on campus in La Crosse, Wisconsin, with teaching assignments that may be offered face-to-face, online, or in a hybrid format. Responsibilities: Teach 12 credit hours per semester, primarily in undergraduate Business, Management, Information Systems, and/or Ethics courses, in face-to-face, online, and/or hybrid formats. Courses may include: Principles of Management, Organizational Behavior, Business Ethics, Strategic Management, Entrepreneurship, Information Systems Other introductory, intermediate, or advanced undergraduate business courses aligned with the candidate's expertise Develop and deliver engaging undergraduate courses that emphasize critical thinking, ethical decision-making, leadership development, and application of business concepts to real-world organizational challenges. Use active and experiential learning approaches, including case studies, applied projects, simulations, team-based learning, community-based projects, and other appropriate instructional methods. Engage in academic advising, student mentoring, and support of students' academic, professional, and leadership development. Collaborate with business faculty and community partners to create and support experiential learning opportunities for undergraduate students. Participate in curriculum development and contribute to the continued development of the College of Business, Leadership, and Ethics undergraduate business programs. Engage with the regional business community and professional organizations to maintain current knowledge of business practices, emerging technologies, and developments in business and management. Engage in service to the department, School, and University. Participate in professional development, including scholarship, applied research, presentations, publications, consulting, or other forms of scholarly and professional engagement appropriate to the faculty member's discipline. Contribute to accreditation, assessment, and continuous improvement activities. Support the mission and values of Viterbo University through teaching, service, mentoring, and engagement with the University community. Qualifications: An earned Doctor of Business Administration (DBA), Ph.D., Ed.D., or other appropriate terminal degree in Business Administration, Management, Organizational Leadership, Information Systems, Business Ethics, or a closely related field is preferred. Candidates who are ABD and have a clear path to terminal degree completion may also be considered. Demonstrated expertise in one or more areas of business, management, organizational behavior, information systems, strategy, entrepreneurship, or ethics. Demonstrated commitment to high-quality undergraduate teaching and student learning. Professional experience in business, management, information systems, consulting, entrepreneurship, nonprofit management, or a related field is desirable. Evidence of effective teaching at the undergraduate level is preferred. Experience incorporating experiential learning, case studies, applied projects, simulations, or other active-learning approaches into undergraduate business education is desirable. Experience teaching face-to-face, online, and/or hybrid formats is preferred. Experience developing or teaching online courses and familiarity with learning management systems and instructional technologies is desirable. Evidence of scholarly or professional engagement appropriate to the candidate's qualifications and discipline is preferred. A demonstrated commitment to undergraduate student success, mentoring, ethical leadership, and values-based education is preferred. Must meet ACBSP accreditation requirements for faculty qualifications. Direct any questions to Dean Nicole Van Ert, Dahl School of Business nmvanert@viterbo.edu. For full consideration, applicants are encouraged to apply by October 30, 2026. Applications will continue to be reviewed until the position is filled. The position will begin in August 2027. To Apply: Please complete the online employment application form and upload a letter of interest highlighting your experiences to support your candidacy., CV/resume, and three professional references. Alignment : Viterbo University seeks employees who will embrace the University mission and incorporate our values into their day-to-day work. Mission: The Viterbo University community prepares students for faithful service and ethical leadership. Values: In keeping with the tradition of our Franciscan founders, we hold the following core values: Contemplation , reflecting upon the presence of God in our lives and work Hospitality , welcoming everyone we encounter as an honored guest Integrity , striving for honesty in everything we say and do Service , working for the common good in the spirit of humility and joy Stewardship , practicing responsible use of all resources in our trust About the University: Viterbo University is a private, not-for-profit, Catholic, Franciscan institutions founded by the Franciscan Sisters of Perpetual Adoration in 1871. Viterbo offers a student-centered liberal arts education with a wide range of undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. Located in La Crosse, Wisconsin, the university is nestled along the scenic Mississippi River and surrounded by the stunning bluffs. The local area combines natural beauty with a vibrant, welcoming community, offering opportunities for outdoor recreation, arts and culture. Together, Viterbo and La Crosse provide an exceptional place to live, work, and make a difference. Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship at this time. The university does not unlawfully discriminate on the basis of sex or engage in sex discrimination in any education program or activity that the university operates. Title IX's mandate not to discriminate on the basis of sex extends to students, employees, applicants for employment, and other persons in all aspects of the university's programs, activities, and operations. Inquiries regarding how Title IX applies to the university may be referred to the university Title IX coordinator, to the U.S. Department of Education Office of Civil Rights, or to both. Contact information for the Title IX coordinator is available at Title IX: Sex and Gender Discrimination or Harassment | Viterbo University"
    },
